two proof problems; 13 is the reserve.  ## Target Problems (in order) See `iterations.md`. Work on exactly ONE unchecked item per iteration.  ## Acceptance Criteria (per item) - [ ] Code lives under `learning/` (or `lean/` for item 12, `satisfiability/`       for a registered heuristic or a flag) with a module docstring saying what       question it answers and how to run it; runnable as `python -m learning.<name>`. - [ ] A section appended to `reports/ml_nature.md` (continuing the numbering,       §28 onwards) with: the question, the method, the baseline, the table(s),       the finding in one paragraph, the size range covered, the kill       criterion's verdict where the plan states one, and the regenerate command. - [ ] `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes (~85 s). New code that computes a       quantity gets at least one test on a tiny hand-checkable instance; a new       flag on the search gets a test that the default path is byte-for-byte       unchanged and a test that the flag never changes a `decide` status. - [ ] The item is marked `- [x]` (done) or `- [!]` (blocked, with a reason in       PROGRESS.md) in `iterations.md`. - [ ] No regressions, no changes to solver defaults, nothing written to       `solutions/`. Generated instances and witnesses go under       `learning/data/ensemble/` (committed; total under ~150 MB apparent).  ## Completion Conditions An item is DONE when either: 1. **Solved**: meets all criteria and the report section is written, OR 2. **Blocked**: documented in PROGRESS.md with the specific blocker. Items 05,    11 and 12 may end with a precise statement of what cannot be done and why;    that is a deliverable, not a failure.  ## Context - **Key files**: `learning/differential.py` (the harness; `--stage drawn`),   `learning/graph_story.py` (relabel, recover), `learning/relabel_portfolio.py`,   `learning/cost_model.py` (pricing for item 07), `learning/ensemble.py` and   `learning/upward.py` (the campaign; resumable), `learning/scale_t