{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KtLUb4hTt2myUL3pHvc6AF","type":"tool_result","content":"45:modeling challenge, SCOOP, Faggioli & Bentvoglio,\n654:                                           • SCOOP [42]. Set of 24 real instances of two sawmilling companies.\n743:                                                    Results for the SCOOP dataset\n744:                                                    The graph shown in Fig 6 contains the results of 24 individual instances of the SCOOP dataset.\n760:      Fig 6. Results for the SCOOP dataset.\n858:                                              Table 3 outlines the results for the proposed dataset with 800×800 and 1000×1000 instances.\n897:Table 3. Results for the new datasets of 800×800 and 1000×1000 instances.\n957:                                               With real SCOOP datasets, whose instances were mostly smaller than 50, PieceRank per-\n1155:                                           42.   SCOOP Project—Sheet Cutting and Process Optimization for furniture enterprises, www.scoop-\n----FIG\ntotal 32\ndrwxrwxr-x   2 al   al      60 Sep 27 17:03 .\ndrwxrwxrwt 141 root root  8360 Sep 27 17:03 ..\n-rw-rw-r--   1 al   al   31794 Sep 27 17:03 fig-000.png\n----DIRS\nChallengeInstances2005\nMOSP_Instances\nbenchmarks/instances/ChallengeInstances2005:\nHarvey\nMiller\nREADME_1.1\nREADME_1.1~\nShaw\nSimonis\nWilson\n\nbenchmarks/instances/MOSP_Instances:\nChallenge\nChu_Stuckey\nFaggioli_Bentivoglio\nS1. Dataset - README FIRST.pdf\nSCOOP\n----API\n302:def _solution_path(instance: MOSPInstance, solutions_dir: Path) -> Path:\n303-    \"\"\"Return the path for a cached solution file.\"\"\"\n304-    # Sanitize instance name for use as a filename\n305-    name = instance.name or \"unnamed\"\n306-    safe_name = \"\".join(c if c.isalnum() or c in \"-_.\" else \"_\" for c in name)\n307-    return solutions_dir / f\"{safe_name}.json\"\n308-\n309-\n310-# How a cached value was established. A corpus that cannot tell a proof from a\n311-# good guess is a liability, and both kinds are now present.\n312-PROVENANCE_REFUTATION = \"certified:refutation\"  # SAT at k, UNSAT at k-1\n313-PROVENANCE_BOUND = \"certified:bound\"            # SAT at k, and lower bound = k\n314-PROVENANCE_RELAXATION = \"certified:relaxation\"  # as above, but the bound came\n38:    def from_file(path: str | Path) -> MOSPInstance:\n65:    def from_matrix(matrix: List[List[int]] | np.ndarray, name: str = \"\") -> MOSPInstance:\n76:    def to_file(self, path: str | Path) -> None:\n84:    def pattern_customers(self, pattern: int) -> set[int]:\n88:    def customer_patterns(self, customer: int) -> set[int]:\n93:    def from_benchmark_file(\n----TIMING\ndef _init_timing(strategies, fold_of_file, model_dir: str) -> None:\n    from satisfiability.heuristics import _learned_model\n\n    _WORK[\"strategies\"] = tuple(strategies)\n    _WORK[\"fold_of_file\"] = fold_of_file\n    _WORK[\"model_dir\"] = Path(model_dir)\n    if MODEL_STRATEGIES & set(strategies):\n        for fold in sorted(set(fold_of_file.values())):\n            _learned_model(_WORK[\"model_dir\"] / f\"fold{fold}.txt\")   # warm the cache\n\n\ndef _time_one(task) -> dict:\n    from satisfiability.heuristics import upper_bound\n\n    source_file, name, n, m, matrix = task\n    instance = MOSPInstance(matrix=np.array(matrix, dtype=np.int8),\n                            n_customers=n, n_patterns=m, name=name)\n    row = {\"instance\": name, \"source_file\": source_file, \"n_customers\": n}\n    for strategy in _WORK[\"strategies\"]:\n        kwargs = {}\n        if strategy in MODEL_STRATEGIES:\n            fold = _WORK[\"fold_of_file\"][source_file]\n            kwargs[\"model_path\"] = str(_WORK[\"model_dir\"] / f\"fold{fold}.txt\")\n        started = time.perf_counter()\n        value, _ = upper_bound(instance, strategy, **kwargs)\n        row[f\"ms:{strategy}\"] = 1000.0 * (time.perf_counter() - started)\n        row[f\"value:{strategy}\"] = value\n    return row\n\n\ndef run_timing(strategies: Sequence[str] = STRATEGIES, workers: int = 16,\n               limit: int | None = None, out: Path = OUT_DIR / \"timing.csv\"\n               ) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Every strategy on every instance in one worker, `perf_counter` around\n    the call. Spawned workers: LightGBM has run in this process by the time\n    the sweep stage is over (CLAUDE.md method note).\"\"\"\n    manifest = json.loads((UNION_MODEL_DIR / \"folds.json\").read_text())\n    pairs = enumerate_instances()\n    if limit:\n        pairs = pairs[:limit]\n    tasks = [(str(path), inst.name, inst.n_customers, inst.n_patterns,\n              inst.matrix.tolist()) for path, inst in pairs]\n    ctx = multiprocessing.get_context(\"spawn\")\n    started = time.time()\n    with ctx.Pool(workers, initializer=_init_timing,\n                  initargs=(tuple(strategies), manifest[\"assignment\"],\n                            str(UNION_MODEL_DIR))) as pool:\n        rows = pool.map(_time_one, tasks, chunksize=8)\n    frame = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    frame.to_csv(out, index=False)\n    print(f\"timed {len(frame)} instances × {len(strategies)} strategies in \"\n          f\"{time.time() - started:.0f}s -> {out}\", flush=True)\n    return frame\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# tables\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_frame(strategies: Sequence[str] = STRATEGIES) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"One row per instance: optimum, each strategy's sweep value, its\n    in-process value and milliseconds, size and collection.\"\"\"\n    frame: pd.DataFrame | None = None\n    for strategy in strategies:\n        data = json.loads(_sweep_path(strategy).read_text())\n        part = pd.DataFrame(data[\"rows\"]).rename(","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9449124f-cac2-4